entities.BreadHelper/FlagOnBerryPickupController.attributes.name.checkGolden=Check for Golden Berry
entities.BreadHelper/FlagOnBerryPickupController.attributes.name.checkMoon=Check for Moon Berry

# DashSpeedWater
entities.BreadHelper/DashSpeedWater.placements.name.DashSpeedWater=Custom Dash Speed Water
entities.BreadHelper/DashSpeedWater.placements.description.DashSpeedWater=Water that allows you to change the dash speed multiplier while dashing in it (vanilla is always 0.75)
entities.BreadHelper/DashSpeedWater.attributes.name.speedMod=Dash Speed Multiplier
entities.BreadHelper/DashSpeedWater.attributes.description.speedMod=The dash speed multiplier when dashing in the water.
entities.BreadHelper/DashSpeedWater.attributes.description.hasBottom=Determines whether or not the water has a bottom.

# ScreenSizedRectangle
entities.BreadHelper/ScreenSizedRectangle.placements.name.ScreenSizedRectangle=Screen Size Rectangle (Lonn only)
entities.BreadHelper/ScreenSizedRectangle.placements.description.ScreenSizedRectangle=A rectangle that is the default screen size. Only appears in Lonn and does nothing in game.

# RevSpeedDashBlock
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.placements.name.RevSpeedDashBlock=Reverse Speed Dash Block
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.placements.description.RevSpeedDashBlock=A dash block that reverses the player's speed when broken. Has many customization options for the directions your speed is flipped.
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.name.HorizontalFlip=Horizontal Side Speed Flip
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.description.HorizontalFlip=Which of the player's speeds get reversed when hitting the horizontal sides of the block.
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.name.VerticalFlip=Vertical Side Speed Flip
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.description.VerticalFlip=Which of the player's speeds get reversed when hitting the vertical sides of the block.
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.name.refillSound=Play Refill Sound
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.description.refillSound=If the refill sound should be played (only activates if Refill Dash is also activated)
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.description.canDash=Whether the player can break the block by dashing into it.
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.description.blendin=Blends the block with the walls it touches, making it less apparent.
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.description.tiletype=Determines the visual appearance of the wall.
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.description.permanent=Once broken, the block will remain that way, even if the player dies.
entities.BreadHelper/RevSpeedDashBlock.attributes.description.breakSound=Sound played when the block breaks.\nMost tilesets use the stone sound, except for dirt, snow, and wood, which use dirt, ice, and wood break sounds respectively.

# SpecialBumper
entities.BreadHelper/SpecialBumper.placements.name.SpecialBumper=Special Bumper
entities.BreadHelper/SpecialBumper.placements.description.SpecialBumper=A bumper with many customizable options and modes, with the unique ones being an option to reverse your speed on hit, an option to only launch in 8 directions, and a customizable dash cooldown.
entities.BreadHelper/SpecialBumper.attributes.description.launchMode=The way the bumper behaves when touched.\nNormal-Functions like vanilla bumpers.\nEight Way-Mostly like vanilla bumpers, but will only launch in 8 set directions.\nReverse Speed-Reverses the player's speed when hit.
entities.BreadHelper/SpecialBumper.attributes.description.dashCooldown=Cooldown before the player can dash again after hitting the bumper.
entities.BreadHelper/SpecialBumper.attributes.description.respawnTime=Time the bumper takes to be reform in order to be hit again.

# TimedDashSwitch
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.placements.name.up=Timed Dash Switch
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.placements.description.up=A dash switch that will unpress itself and close the opened door after a certain time. Can also set a flag while pressed.
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.placements.description.down=A dash switch that will unpress itself and close the opened door after a certain time. Can also set a flag while pressed.
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.placements.description.left=A dash switch that will unpress itself and close the opened door after a certain time. Can also set a flag while pressed.
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.placements.description.right=A dash switch that will unpress itself and close the opened door after a certain time. Can also set a flag while pressed.
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.attributes.description.sprite=Changes the visual appearance of the switch.
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.attributes.description.allGates=Whether the switch should open all temple gates instead of opening only the closest one.
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.attributes.description.flag=The flag that is set while the switch is pressed. If it is empty, no flag will be set.
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.attributes.description.time=How long the switch stays pressed before resetting.
entities.BreadHelper/TimedDashSwitch.attributes.description.openFast=Whether the temple gate should play its full opening animation that it usually does or open faster.

# AngledCloud
entities.BreadHelper/AngledCloud.placements.name.normal=Arbitrary Angle Cloud
entities.BreadHelper/AngledCloud.placements.description.normal=A cloud that can move at any angle instead of just down then up.
entities.BreadHelper/AngledCloud.attributes.description.fragile=Determines whether the cloud will temporarily disappear after being touched.
entities.BreadHelper/AngledCloud.attributes.description.small=Reduces the surface area of the cloud.
entities.BreadHelper/AngledCloud.attributes.description.angle=The angle at which the cloud launches. Vanilla (launch straight up) is 90 degrees.
entities.BreadHelper/AngledCloud.attributes.description.hasArrow=Whether or not to display an arrow that indicated the direction.

# DashMoveBlock
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.placements.name.DashMoveBlock=Dash Move Block
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.placements.description.DashMoveBlock=A move block that will activate when dashed into. Also has the option to activate by standing but not until it has been dashed into.
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.attributes.description.canSteer=Determines whether the move block can be moved by the player.
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.attributes.description.speed=The speed of the move block. Vanilla "fast" is 75, and "slow" is 60.
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.attributes.description.startupTime=The time the move block shakes once activated before it starts moving.
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.attributes.description.direction=Determines the direction the move block moves in upon activation.
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.attributes.description.triggerOnDash=Whether the block will immediately activate on being dashed into, or wait until it is stood on after.
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.attributes.description.fixDepth=Gives the move block a normal depth value so it doesn't have inconsistent layering with spikes.
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.attributes.description.breakSound=Sound played when the block is first dashed into.
entities.BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock.attributes.description.borderTexture=The texture of the border. Put the image in Graphics/Atlases/Gameplay/objects/BreadHelper/DashMoveBlock/texturename.png, with texturename in this field. See the defualt image to see how to format it. This will not apply in lonn sorry, :P.

# BufferFixSpring
entities.BreadHelper/BufferFixSpring.placements.name.BufferFixSpring=Buffer Fix Spring
entities.BreadHelper/BufferFixSpring.placements.description.BufferFixSpring=Buffer Fix Spring=A spring that will not apply forcemove if you dash right after hitting it. Also supports down facing cause I felt like it.
entities.BreadHelper/BufferFixSpring.attributes.description.playerCanUse=Determines whether the player is able to interact with the spring.

# MirrorCustomizer
entities.BreadHelper/MirrorCustomizer.placements.name.MirrorCustomizer=Mirror Customizer
entities.BreadHelper/MirrorCustomizer.placements.description.MirrorCustomizer=An entity that allows you to give/take away reflections to/from any given entity that is inside this entity.
entities.BreadHelper/MirrorCustomizer.attributes.description.RemoveMirror=Comma seperated list of entities to remove reflections from. Enter the name given at the top of the box in lonn for this field, not the class name.
entities.BreadHelper/MirrorCustomizer.attributes.description.AddMirror=Comma seperated list of entities to give reflections to. Enter the name given at the top of the box in lonn for this field, not the class name.
entities.BreadHelper/MirrorCustomizer.attributes.description.RemoveMirrorByClass=Comma seperated list of entities to remove reflections from. This field uses class names to affect particular entities that are not directly placeable in lonn.
entities.BreadHelper/MirrorCustomizer.attributes.description.AddMirrorByClass=Comma seperated list of entities to give reflections to. This field uses class names to affect particular entities that are not directly placeable in lonn.
entities.BreadHelper/MirrorCustomizer.attributes.description.updateFlag=When this flag is set, this entity will re-check what entities are inside it and apply/remove reflections accordingly.